Let me look at the `rans_decode` function to understand the potential double-free. But first, let me think about the actual vulnerability more carefully. The crash state is `decode_names -> cram_uncompress_block -> cram_read_SAM_hdr`. The double-free is in `decode_names`.

Let me look at the copy path once more. The key issue might be in the `memcpy` when `ctx->desc[j].buf` is NULL but `ctx->desc[i].buf_a` is non-zero. But that would be a NULL deref, not double-free.

Actually, let me reconsider. The `free_context` function frees `desc[i].buf` for `i < max_tok*16`. If `max_tok` is set to a value, and then later `tnum` is incremented again with `memset(&ctx->desc[tnum<<4], 0, ...)`, that zeroes out the descriptors. But `max_tok` is updated to `tnum+1`. So `free_context` frees `desc[0]` through `desc[(tnum+1)*16 - 1]`.

Now, the double-free could happen if the same buffer pointer appears in two `desc[i].buf` slots. Let me look at the copy path again:

```c
i = (tnum<<4) | (ttype&15);
if (j >= i)
    goto err;

ctx->desc[i].buf_l = 0;
ctx->desc[i].buf_a = ctx->desc[j].buf_a;
if (ctx->desc[i].buf) free(ctx->desc[i].buf);
ctx->desc[i].buf = malloc(ctx->desc[i].buf_a);
if (!ctx->desc[i].buf)
    goto err;

memcpy(ctx->desc[i].buf, ctx->desc[j].buf, ctx->desc[i].buf_a);
```

This makes a copy. So `desc[i].buf` and `desc[j].buf` are distinct. No aliasing.

Hmm, but wait. What about the "Load compressed block" path where `ttype&128` is set and `ttype&15 != 0`:

```c
if ((ttype & 15) != 0 && (ttype & 128)) {
    if (ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf) free(ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf);
    ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf = malloc(nreads);
    if (!ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf)
        goto err;
    ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf_l = 0;
    ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf_a = nreads;
    ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf[0] = ttype&15;
    memset(&ctx->desc[tnum<<4].buf[1], N_MATCH, nreads-1);
}
```

This allocates `desc[tnum<<4].buf`. Then later:
```c
i = (tnum<<4) | (ttype&15);
if (i >= MAX_TBLOCKS || i < 0)
    goto err;

ctx->desc[i].buf_l = 0;
if (ctx->desc[i].buf) free(ctx->desc[i].buf);
ctx->desc[i].buf = malloc(ulen);
```

Since `ttype&15 != 0`, `i != tnum<<4`. So `desc[i].buf` is a different slot. Fine.

